DSperate on macOS (Apple Silicon), applied to third_party/dsperate-lr/DSperate by
third_party/patches/apply_dsperate_macos_patch.cmake when building on Apple only:
- crypto/aes.c: no <sys/auxv.h>/getauxval on macOS; every Apple Silicon core has the AES instructions.
- cheat/analog_db.cpp, io/dsi_font.cpp, gpu/gl/gl_shaders.cpp, gpu/vk/vk_shaders.cpp: the .incbin blobs go in
  Mach-O's __TEXT,__const and their symbols carry the leading underscore C names have there.
- gpu/render3d.cpp: Apple clang refuses reinterpret_cast from const void* to a function pointer (const_cast first).
- gpu/kernels_neon.cpp: Apple's vst1_u32 is a macro, so a brace-initialised vector argument needs parentheses.
- cpu/jit (the recompiler, on since Mac 3): the code arena is MAP_JIT and every write to it sits in a JitWriteScope
  (pthread_jit_write_protect_np: a thread sees MAP_JIT memory writable or executable, never both); dispatch loads the
  arena base as a constant instead of keeping it in x18, which macOS reserves; the fastmem fault handler reads Darwin's
  ucontext. mem/fastmem.cpp: fastmem stays off (no memfd; its views have no macOS backing), so the recompiler takes its
  page-table path.

